## B. SECURITY ISSUES

| # | File | Problem | Risk | Fix |
|---|------|---------|------|-----|
| S1 | `.env` | Live Supabase anon key and Razorpay test key in `.env` | **Medium** — anon key is public by design (RLS protects data), but key rotation recommended if repo was ever shared | Add comment to `.env.example` clarifying these are public keys |
| S2 | `create-razorpay-order/index.ts` | CORS `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` | **Medium** — allows any domain to invoke the edge function | Restrict to application domain |
| S3 | `admin-manage-role/index.ts` | CORS `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` | **Medium** | Restrict to application domain |
| S4 | `Login.tsx` | No client-side rate limiting on login/signup/forgot forms | **High** — rapid form submission possible | Add submission cooldown and debounce |
| S5 | `Login.tsx` | Password field has no show/hide toggle | **Low** — UX issue, not security | Add eye toggle |
| S6 | `ResetPassword.tsx` | No loading state, no submission protection | **Medium** — double submission possible | Add loading state |
| S7 | `Checkout.tsx` | Order can be placed by unauthenticated users — order row exposes `customer_name`, `customer_email`, `customer_phone` in DB | **Low** — by design (guest checkout), but RLS policy `orders_insert_any` allows any insert | Acceptable for guest checkout |
| S8 | `upload.ts` | Extension derived from user filename only (`.pop()`) — no MIME validation on server | **Medium** — Supabase Storage handles MIME, but client should also validate | Improve client-side validation |
| S9 | `index.html` | No CSP meta tag | **Medium** | Add Content-Security-Policy |
| S10 | `Checkout.tsx` | Discount code validation happens client-side against DB — no server-side check that discount was valid at time of order | **Medium** — user could manipulate discount amount | Validate in edge function |
| S11 | `Reviews.tsx` | Comment field has no max length — XSS risk if rendered unsanitized | **Low** — React auto-escapes JSX | Add maxLength |
| S12 | `AuthContext.tsx:47` | Silent `catch {}` on profile upsert — swallows auth errors | **Low** | Log warning |

